# MILESTONE 1 — STABILIZE THE APPLICATION

## Priority: Fix the WatchPage Hooks error first

The existing application has reported this React error:

"React has detected a change in the order of Hooks called by WatchPage."

The error log indicated that the previous render and next render differed around Hook 58, where a `useCallback` appeared in the next render.

The reported location was approximately:

`src/pages/Watch/WatchPage.tsx:473`

The exact cause must be confirmed by inspecting the source code.

### Required investigation

Inspect:

- `src/pages/Watch/WatchPage.tsx`
- All hooks inside `WatchPage`
- All conditional branches
- All early returns
- All loading states
- All error states
- All callbacks
- All effects
- All custom hooks used by the component

Identify why the number or order of hooks changes between renders.

### Required fix

Ensure every React hook is called unconditionally and in the same order on every render.

If necessary:

- Move hooks above conditional returns.
- Move conditional logic inside effects or callbacks.
- Extract independent UI sections into child components.
- Correct hook dependencies.
- Remove duplicated or unnecessary hooks.
- Preserve existing component functionality.

Do not disable React StrictMode.

Do not suppress the error.

Do not hide the error using a try/catch.

Do not rewrite the entire WatchPage unnecessarily.

### Test the following states

- Initial loading
- Anime details loaded
- Episode list loaded
- Provider loading
- Provider failure
- Missing episode
- Episode switching
- Navigation away from WatchPage
- Returning to WatchPage
- Browser back and forward
- Component re-rendering
- Empty and error states

### Milestone 1 acceptance criteria

- No React Hooks order errors.
- No new console errors.
- Existing routes still work.
- Existing streaming functionality remains intact.
- TypeScript checks pass.
- Production build succeeds.
- Existing functionality is preserved.

Do not proceed with the visual redesign until this milestone is stable.

