# MILESTONE 5 — STREAMING ENGINE AND EPISODE DISCOVERY

This is a critical milestone.

Inspect the current streaming architecture and all existing providers before making changes.

The goal is to improve actual playback reliability, not merely make the player look better.

## Provider architecture

Create or improve a modular provider system.

Each provider should have a consistent interface for:

- Provider identification
- Anime lookup
- Episode discovery
- Episode mapping
- Stream source resolution
- Subtitle information
- Audio information
- Provider health
- Error reporting
- Timeout handling

Keep provider-specific logic isolated.

Do not allow one failing provider to break the entire watch page.

## Existing provider audit

Inspect all existing provider integrations.

Determine:

- Which providers are configured
- Which providers are actually reachable
- Which providers return valid anime results
- Which providers return episode lists
- Which providers return playable streams
- Which providers fail due to CORS
- Which providers fail due to API changes
- Which providers are blocked by the browser
- Which providers are unsupported

Do not mark a provider active merely because its name appears in the code.

Do not invent endpoints or assume undocumented APIs work.

## Provider failover

When a provider fails:

1. Record the failure.
2. Identify whether the failure is temporary or permanent.
3. Attempt another available provider when appropriate.
4. Preserve the selected anime and episode.
5. Avoid unnecessary repeated requests.
6. Inform the user when all available sources fail.

Provider failover must not create infinite loops.

## Episode discovery

Fix incomplete episode lists.

Support:

- Independent episode discovery
- Multiple provider episode lists
- Episode deduplication
- Episode number normalization
- Episode title preservation
- Episode ordering
- Provider-specific identifiers
- Special episodes where identifiable
- Missing metadata
- Pagination where supported

Merge provider episode results carefully.

Do not invent episodes.

Do not assume every anime has the same episode numbering system.

Do not discard valid episodes simply because one provider returns fewer episodes.

## Timeout and retry handling

Address existing errors such as:

"Request timed out after 10 seconds."

Implement:

- Configurable timeouts
- AbortController cancellation where supported
- Retry with exponential backoff
- Limited retry counts
- Independent provider requests
- Partial results
- Request deduplication
- Caching
- Clear error messages

Do not allow one slow provider to block all other providers.

Do not retry indefinitely.

## Caching

Cache appropriate data such as:

- Anime metadata
- Episode lists
- Provider results
- Search results
- Provider health information

Use suitable expiration times.

Avoid caching temporary failures as though they were successful results.

Invalidate caches when necessary.

## Streaming source resolution

Inspect each source for:

- Valid URL
- Supported format
- HLS or DASH compatibility
- Audio tracks
- Subtitle tracks
- CORS restrictions
- Browser codec support
- Expired links
- Redirect behavior

Do not fabricate playable URLs.

### Acceptance criteria

- Episode discovery is more complete.
- Providers fail independently.
- Timeouts are handled gracefully.
- Valid episodes are deduplicated.
- No fabricated episodes or stream links.
- Provider errors are visible and actionable.
- Existing working providers remain functional.

