For every milestone, follow this exact process.

## Step 1 — Inspect

Inspect the relevant files, components, APIs, state, routes, and dependencies.

Identify the existing implementation before editing.

## Step 2 — Report

Briefly explain:

- What is currently implemented
- What is broken
- The root cause of the issue
- Which files need changes
- Any risks to existing functionality

Do not guess the root cause.

## Step 3 — Implement

Make the smallest safe set of changes that fully addresses the milestone.

Preserve unrelated functionality.

Avoid unnecessary rewrites.

## Step 4 — Test

Run all relevant available checks, including:

- TypeScript
- Lint
- Production build
- Relevant tests
- Browser interaction tests where available

If a test cannot be run, state that clearly.

## Step 5 — Fix

Resolve errors introduced by the implementation.

Do not leave known regressions unresolved.

## Step 6 — Report completion

Provide:

- Milestone number and name
- Files changed
- Features implemented
- Tests run
- Actual test results
- Remaining limitations
- Whether the milestone meets its acceptance criteria

Only mark a milestone complete when it has been verified.

